. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         * only keep participants with at least one child 
.         keep if inlist(kidsex01, 1, 2)
(10,637 observations deleted)

.         
.         * only keep participants with a reply on political attitudes 
.         keep if inrange(plh0004, 0,10)
(21,091 observations deleted)

. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * generate dummy variable for whether participant's first child is fe
> male (1) or not (0)
.         gen byte d_daughter = kidsex01 == 2 

.         
.         * generate left-leaning political preferences 0-10 (less to more left
> -leaning)
.         gen left_leaning = 10 - plh0004 

. 
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. *** H2: Having daughters leads to more left-leaning political preferences. **
> *  
. 
.         /* Verbal description of your model: Gender of first child is exogene
> ous, later children may be endogeneous. Regress the outcome on dummy variable
>  indicating whether the first child is a daughter, for parents. Include indic
> ators for survey years because of time trends and because some outcomes may b
> e combinations of variables from different years. Cluster standard errors on 
> individual respondent.  */ 
. 
.         * Regression  
. 
.         reg left_leaning d_daughter i.syear, vce(cl pid)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =      3,500
                                                F(4, 1860)        =       5.14
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0004
                                                R-squared         =     0.0065
                                                Root MSE          =     1.6619

                                (Std. err. adjusted for 1,861 clusters in pid)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
left_leaning | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
  d_daughter |   .1735207   .0760482     2.28   0.023      .024372    .3226694
             |
       syear |
       2009  |  -.0025489   .0668281    -0.04   0.970    -.1336148    .1285171
       2014  |   .2244819   .0718148     3.13   0.002     .0836359     .365328
       2019  |   .1731499   .0753307     2.30   0.022     .0254082    .3208915
             |
       _cons |   5.044377   .0697293    72.34   0.000     4.907621    5.181133
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * (Please check whether the suggested code autom
> atically picks up the correct statistics for your chosen regression analysis 
> and adapt if needed)
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[d_daughter] / _se[d_daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
.         // Display the saved statistics
